  "prefLabel": "Lot 7202.14 Games of Chance (GOC)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lot 7202.14 “Games of Chance (GOC)” means “games of chance” as defined in RSA 287-D:1, III, namely “any game involving gambling as defined by RSA 647:2,II, or any lottery prohibited by RSA 647:1, but shall not include any game involving the use of a slot machine or any other device in the nature of a slot machine, 50/50 raffles as defined in RSA 287-A:1,III, or ice-out contests as defined in RSA 287-D:1, VI.” For the purposes of this chapter, this term refers only to GOC that are typically offered at casinos, such as poker and its variations, roulette, blackjack, craps, money wheel, baccarat, and sic bo, and other such games authorized by the commission. This term does not include sports betting, or VLTs.\n\nSource. #12839, eff 7-27-19; ss by #14341, EMERGENCY, eff 8-21-25 (formerly Lot 7202.04); ss by #14503, eff 2-4-26, EXPIRES: 2-4-36 (formerly Lot 7202.09)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lot7200.html"
